defaultdescascmultiple columns <pre><code>await Actor().orderBy('name').get();
</code></pre> <pre><code>await Actor().orderBy('name', 'desc').get();
</code></pre> <pre><code>await Actor().orderBy('name', 'asc').get();
</code></pre> <pre><code>await Actor()
    .orderBy('name', 'asc')
    .orderBy('id', 'desc')
    .get();
</code></pre> <p>Info</p> <p>The direction must be <code>asc</code> or <code>desc</code>. Any other value throws an <code>ArgumentError</code>. The column name is quoted, but a name with <code>(</code> is kept as it is. Do not pass user input as the column name.</p>

TransactionReturn a valueOther connection <pre><code>await QueryBuilder.transaction(() async {
    Actor actor = Actor();
    actor.name = 'John Wick';
    await actor.save();
    await QueryBuilder.table('actor_info').insert({'actor_id': actor.id});
});
</code></pre> <pre><code>int id = await QueryBuilder.transaction(() async {
    Actor actor = Actor();
    actor.name = 'John Wick';
    await actor.save();
    return actor.id;
});
</code></pre> <pre><code>await QueryBuilder.transaction(() async {
    // ...
}, connection: 'mysql');
</code></pre> <ul> <li>All queries and models inside the function use the transaction.</li> <li>A transaction inside another transaction joins the outer one.</li> </ul> <p>MySQL</p> <p><code>CREATE</code>, <code>ALTER</code> and <code>DROP TABLE</code> commit right away on MySQL. A rollback can not undo them.</p>

