beforeSavebeforeGet <pre><code>@DoxModel()
class Blog extends BlogGenerator {
    @column(beforeSave: getSlugFromTitle)
    String? slug

    static getSlugFromTitle(Map&lt;String, dynamic&gt; map) {
        return slugify(map['title']);
    }
}
</code></pre> <pre><code>@DoxModel()
class Blog extends BlogGenerator {
    @column(name: 'published_at', beforeGet: convertToHumanReadable)
    DateTime? publishedAt

    static convertToHumanReadable(Map&lt;String, dynamic&gt; map) {
        var format = DateFormat.yMd('us');
        var dateString = format.format(DateTime.parse(map['published_at']));
    }
}
</code></pre> <p>Warning</p> <p><code>beforeSave</code> and <code>beforeGet</code> hook must be static function inside Model class.</p>

Save a new recordSet a field to null <pre><code>Blog blog = Blog();
blog.title = 'title';
await blog.save();
</code></pre> <pre><code>Blog? blog = await Blog().find(1);
blog?.slug = null;
await blog?.save(); // slug is now NULL in the database
</code></pre> <p>Info</p> <p>On insert, <code>null</code> fields are not sent, so the database default is used. On update, a field is set to <code>NULL</code> only when it had a value before (loaded from the database or saved). Fields that were not loaded, for example with <code>select()</code>, are not changed.</p>

Delete a recordRestore a soft deleted record <pre><code>Blog? blog = await Blog().find(1);
await blog?.delete(); // only deletes this record
</code></pre> <pre><code>Blog? blog = await Blog().withTrash().find(1);
await blog?.restore(); // sets deleted_at back to NULL
</code></pre> <p>Info</p> <p><code>save()</code>, <code>delete()</code>, <code>forceDelete()</code> and <code>restore()</code> fire model events.</p>

Debug <pre><code>Blog blog = blog();
blog.debug(true);
blog.name = 'John Wick';
await blog.save();
</code></pre> <p>Info</p> <p>Debug <code>true</code> option will print the SQL query in the console/terminal.</p>

